  "title": "Antichains in the cycle continuous order",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "If $G$, $H$ are graphs, a function $f: E(G) \\rightarrow E(H)$ is called cycle-continuous if the pre-image of every element of the (binary) cycle space of $H$ is a member of the cycle space of $G$.\n\nProblem Does there exist an infinite set of graphs $\\{G_1,G_2,\\ldots \\}$ so that there is no cycle continuous mapping between $G_i$ and $G_j$ whenever $i \\neq j$?",
